PROSE = {
4255: "*And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name Yahusha (JESUS): for he shall save his people from their sins* (Matthew 1:21). The name given at the manger had already been named before the Head of Days. Enoch saw the Son of Adam named in the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits before there was a Bethlehem to be born in; the angel's instruction to Yoseph (Joseph) is that name arriving on earth. The one who saves his people is the one who was named before his people existed.",
4257: "*They shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, Elohim (God) with us* (Matthew 1:23). Chosen and hidden before the creation of the world — then revealed in flesh. The Formed one, drawn from the Father before anything was made, is the one Matthew calls *Elohim (God) with us.* He was not new at the manger; he was hidden, and the hiding ended.",
4390: "*The foxes have holes, and the birds of the air have nests; but the Son of Adam hath not where to lay his head* (Matthew 8:20). This is where the title comes from. Enoch saw the Head of Days, white-haired, and beside him one with the face of a man and the graciousness of a holy angel, and asked who he was. When Yahusha (Jesus) calls himself the Son of Adam, he is naming himself as the one who stood beside the Head of Days — and that one now has no bed on the earth he came to.",
4392: "*The Son of Adam hath not where to lay his head* (Matthew 8:20). The angel answered Enoch's question by title and by role: the Son of Adam who has righteousness, who reveals what is hidden, whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits has chosen, whose lot has the pre-eminence for ever. That is the figure Yahusha (Jesus) names himself as. The pre-eminent one before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits is the homeless one on the road to Capernaum, and both are the same Son of Adam.",
4409: "*The Son of Adam hath power on earth to forgive sins* (Matthew 9:6). The scribes called it blasphemy because only Yahuah (God) forgives. Enoch had already seen this Son of Adam named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, before the Head of Days — named, not made. The power exercised over a palsied man in Capernaum is the standing of the one who was named before creation, now exercised in flesh. The scribes were right about who forgives; they were wrong about who stood in front of them.",
4455: "*I am come to set a man at variance against his father, and the daughter against her mother* (Matthew 10:35). Enoch saw the household come apart in the day of destruction — parents carrying off and abandoning their own children, no pity for their beloved. The King says the same division will run through the household when his voice is heard, because some in the house will hear and some will not. The line does not stop at the front door.",
4456: "*And a man's foes shall be they of his own household* (Matthew 10:36). The King is quoting Micah: *a man's enemies are the men of his own house* (Micah 7:6). Enoch saw it in blood — fathers and sons smitten in one place, brother falling on brother from dawn till sunset. The seed war of Genesis 3:15 runs inside families, not only between nations; two brunettes can bear a son of Belial, and Eli's own sons were sons of Belial. Hearing the Shepherd's voice divides a house because not everyone in the house is a sheep.",
4481: "*No man knoweth the Son, but the Father; neither knoweth any man the Father, save the Son* (Matthew 11:27). Enoch saw the two together before the incarnation: One with a head of days, and with him another whose face was like a man's and full of grace. The Father and the Son, side by side, in a vision written centuries before Matthew. What the King says in prayer — that the Father and the Son know each other as no one else does — Enoch saw as a picture: the two of them, together, and no third.",
4482: "*Neither knoweth any man the Father, save the Son, and he to whomsoever the Son will reveal him* (Matthew 11:27). The angel told Enoch what the Son of Adam does: he *revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden,* because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits chose him. The Father is the hidden treasure; the Son is the one who reveals him, and he reveals him to whom he will. Enoch is told this by title; the King says it in the first person.",
4483: "*No man knoweth the Son, but the Father* (Matthew 11:27). Chosen and hidden before him, before the creation of the world — the Son was known to the Father before anyone else existed to know him. That is why no one knows the Son but the Father: the knowing began before the world did. The disciples would come to know him later; the Father's knowing has no beginning.",
4484: "*Thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes* (Matthew 11:25). Enoch says who the revealing is for: the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits reveals him *to the holy and righteous,* the ones who have hated this world of unrighteousness and all its ways. Not the credentialed, not the wise in their own eyes — the ones whose lot he preserved. The babes of Matthew 11:25 are the holy and righteous of 1 Enoch 48:7. The revealing does not make them his; it finds them already his.",
4502: "*Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him* (Matthew 12:18). Matthew is quoting Isaiah 42:1 over the Galilean ministry. Enoch saw the same anointing from the other side of the veil: wisdom poured out on the Elect One like water, glory that does not fail, might in all the secrets of righteousness. The Spirit the Father put upon his servant at the river is the wisdom Enoch saw poured out on the one who stands before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.",
4503: "*I will put my spirit upon him* (Matthew 12:18). Isaiah named what that Spirit is: *the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of Yahuah (LORD)* (Isaiah 11:2). Enoch names the same spirits dwelling in the Elect One — wisdom, insight, understanding and might — and adds one Isaiah did not: *the spirit of those who have fallen asleep in righteousness.* The anointed one carries the righteous dead with him. Three witnesses, one Spirit, one anointed.",
4508: "*How can one enter into a strong man's house, and spoil his goods, except he first bind the strong man?* (Matthew 12:29). Binding is how Yahuah (God) deals with the strong man. Raphael was sent to bind Azazel hand and foot, cast him into darkness, cover him with rocks, and leave him there until the judgment. When Yahusha (Jesus) cast out devils and said the strong man had to be bound first, he was describing something that had been done before and would be done again — the binding of the serpent for the length of the reign (Revelation 20:2). The exorcisms were the spoiling; the binding is older than Galilee.",
4509: "*Except he first bind the strong man* (Matthew 12:29). Enoch asked what the chains were for and was told: for the hosts of Azazel, to cast them into the abyss of complete condemnation with their jaws covered in stones. The chains were already forged when the King spoke of binding. The spoiling of the strong man's house in Galilee is the beginning of what those chains were made for.",
4518: "*So shall the Son of Adam be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth* (Matthew 12:40). The heart of the earth gives back. Enoch saw the earth return what was entrusted to it, Sheol give back what it received, hell give back what it owes. The sign of Jonah is a man going into the deep and being given back; the Son of Adam went into the heart of the earth knowing the earth would have to return him, because the earth returns what it holds.",
4535: "*But while men slept, his enemy came and sowed tares among the wheat* (Matthew 13:25). Here is the sowing. In the days of Jared the children of heaven looked on the daughters of men and took wives, and a seed entered the field that was not of Adam. The enemy sowed while men slept; Enoch tells you who the enemy was and what he sowed. The parable is not a figure of speech. It is the history of Genesis 6 told as a field.",
4537: "*The tares are the children of the wicked one* (Matthew 13:38). The children of the wicked one have a father and a beginning. Enoch names it: the giants born of spirits and flesh became evil spirits on the earth when their bodies died, and evil spirits they are called. The tares are not bad wheat; they are another seed with another origin, and the spirits of that seed are still at work in the field. The parable names them; 1 Enoch names where they came from.",
4542: "*Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father* (Matthew 13:43). Enoch says it to the righteous directly: you were put to shame, and now you shall shine as the lights of heaven, you shall be seen, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to you. Daniel says the same (Daniel 12:3). The shining is not a reward for effort; it is what happens to the righteous when the shame is lifted at the harvest.",
4544: "*I will utter things which have been kept secret from the foundation of the world* (Matthew 13:35). The one speaking in parables was himself the secret kept from the foundation of the world — chosen and hidden before the creation, and for evermore. When he opens his mouth in parables he is the hidden one revealing hidden things. The secret and the one who tells it are the same.",
4554: "*The angels shall come forth, and sever the wicked from among the just* (Matthew 13:49). The angels who sever at the end are the angels who guard until the end. Enoch saw holy angels set over the righteous as guardians, keeping them as the apple of an eye until all wickedness is done away, so that the righteous sleep without fear. The same hands that guard the just through the age are the hands that separate the wicked from them at the harvest.",
4599: "*Thou art the Messiah (Christ), the Son of the living Elohim (God)* (Matthew 16:16). Kefa (Peter) names him on earth. Enoch saw him named in heaven — the Son of Adam named in the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, before the Head of Days. The confession at Caesarea Philippi did not give him the name; it recognized a name that was given before the world was made.",
4600: "*Flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 16:17). What the Father revealed to Kefa (Peter) was old: *before the sun and the signs were created, before the stars of the heaven were made, his name was named.* The revealing did not create a truth; it uncovered one older than the stars. That is why Yahusha (Jesus) credits the Father and not Kefa — the Father is the one who named him in the first place.",
4613: "*The gates of hell shall not prevail against it* (Matthew 16:18). The gates of Sheol cannot hold because Sheol has to give back. Enoch saw the earth return what was entrusted to it, Sheol give back what it received, and hell give back what it owes. The assembly built on the rock is built on a resurrection; the gates that could not hold him cannot hold his own.",
4678: "*Woe unto the world because of offences! for it must needs be that offences come* (Matthew 18:7). Why must they come? Because the whole earth was corrupted through what Azazel taught, and the corruption is still running. Enoch says *to him ascribe all sin.* Offences are inevitable in a corrupted world — and that inevitability excuses no one, which is why the King's woe lands on the man by whom the offence comes. The earth is defiled under its inhabitants, as Isaiah said (Isaiah 24:5–6), and every man who adds to the defiling answers for his part.",
4679: "*But woe to that man by whom the offence cometh!* (Matthew 18:7). Uriel showed Enoch the angels who joined themselves to women, and said their spirits, taking many forms, *lead them astray* — into sacrificing to demons as gods. Leading astray is the offence. Every system that teaches the little ones to walk contrary to the Father's commandments is doing what those spirits do, in whatever form the age gives it. The little ones led astray are victims; the woe is for the ones doing the leading.",
4681: "*It is better for thee to enter into life with one eye, rather than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire* (Matthew 18:9). The hell fire the King names is Gehenna — the valley on the south side of Jerusalem. Enoch was shown that valley before the city had a name for it: *this accursed valley is for those who are accursed for ever,* where those who speak hard things against Yahuah (Lord) are gathered for judgment. The place of judgment is a real place, and it is the place where the judgment is carried out; that is why a man cuts off what makes him stumble.",
4684: "*It is not the will of your Father which is in heaven, that one of these little ones should perish* (Matthew 18:14). Enoch saw lambs born to the white sheep begin to open their eyes and see, and cry to the sheep. The Father's will for the little ones is that they open their eyes. The ones who open them are the ones who could — the lambs who were sheep's lambs. The Father does not lose what is his; what is his hears when he calls.",
4714: "*Who then can be saved?* (Matthew 19:25). The disciples asked it because the rich had always looked blessed. Enoch had already answered: *ye know no ransom.* Riches are no ransom on the day of the great judgment; the sinner who trusted them departs and dies. If the thing everyone counted as blessing cannot save, then no one can be saved by what he has — which is the point the King makes in the next verse: with men impossible, with Elohim (God) possible.",
4727: "*For many be called, but few chosen* (Matthew 20:16). Enoch saw the fountain: inexhaustible righteousness, many fountains of wisdom around it, and *all the thirsty drank.* The call goes out wide because the thirsty are scattered and no one knows them by sight. But the verse ends with where the drinkers lived — *with the righteous and holy and elect.* Many drink; the ones whose dwelling was already with the elect are the few. The call reveals who was chosen; it does not make the choice.",
4734: "*The Son of Adam came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many* (Matthew 20:28). The one who gives his life is the one Enoch was told about by title: the Son of Adam who has righteousness, chosen by Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, whose lot has the pre-eminence for ever. The title is not a humble word for *human.* It is the name of the pre-eminent one, and the pre-eminent one came to serve.",
4735: "*To give his life a ransom for many* (Matthew 20:28). The ransom was not an accident of history. The Son of Adam who gave it was named before the Head of Days, before the sun and the stars; John calls him *the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world* (Revelation 13:8). He walked into the ransom knowing it, because it was settled before there was a world to ransom.",
4780: "*What think ye of Messiah (Christ)? whose son is he? They say unto him, The Son of David* (Matthew 22:42). Right as far as it goes. The Messiah is David's son by the promise to David. But Enoch was shown a Son of Adam whose lot has the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits *for ever* — before David, before Adam's line reached David at all. The Pharisees had the half the Tanakh gave them. The other half was in a book the scribes did not read from.",
4781: "*How then doth David in spirit call him Adonai (Lord)?* (Matthew 22:43). David calls his own descendant *my Lord* because the descendant is older than the ancestor. Enoch saw the Son of Adam named before the Head of Days — before David's line existed, before any line existed. The Pharisees could not answer the question because they did not have this verse. David, in the Spirit, did.",
4791: "*Ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than yourselves* (Matthew 23:15). Enoch's woe is the same woe: on those who pervert the words of uprightness, transgress the eternal law, and *transform themselves into what they were not.* The proselyte is transformed into something — and what he is transformed into is a sinner wearing Torah's name, because the ones who made him teach contrary to the Torah they claim. *He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar* (1 John 2:4). The test is old.",
4806: "*But as the days of Noe were, so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be* (Matthew 24:37). Enoch tells you what the days of Noah were. A messenger was sent to Noah in Yahuah's (the Lord's) name: hide yourself, the end is approaching, a deluge is coming on the whole earth. The earth was corrupted by the Watchers' works, the judgment was announced to one man, and the flood came on the rest. The coming of the Son of Adam is that pattern again: a corrupted earth, a warning carried by the few, and a day the many do not see coming.",
4811: "*For as the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west; so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be* (Matthew 24:27). Nothing secret about it. Enoch saw hosts on wagons coming on the winds from the east and from the west — a coming that fills the sky from one side to the other. The King gives the same picture: lightning, east to west, seen by everyone. Whatever the pulpit sells as a quiet disappearance, the coming of the Son of Adam is a sky-wide event.",
4812: "*And they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other* (Matthew 24:31). *From one end of heaven to the other* is Enoch's phrase before it is Matthew's: when the wagons came, the sound was heard *from the one end of heaven to the other, in one day.* The gathering of the elect is loud and whole-sky — the twelve tribes brought back from wherever they were driven (Deuteronomy 30:4; Ezekiel 37:21), with a sound that moves the pillars of the earth.",
4813: "*They shall gather together his elect from the four winds* (Matthew 24:31). The gathering reaches the ones no one could find. Enoch saw the measures reveal the secrets of the depths of the earth — those destroyed in the desert, devoured by beasts, devoured by the fish of the sea — *that they may return,* on the day of the Elect One, *for none shall be destroyed before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The seed scattered into the sea and the wilderness is not lost to him. The four winds give back what they took.",
4851: "*Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Matthew 26:64). He said it to the men who were about to sentence him. Enoch saw what that Son of Adam does to men in seats of power: he raises the kings and the mighty from their seats and breaks the teeth of the sinners. The council that judged him will be raised from its seats by him. The verdict on the night was the Sanhedrin's; the verdict that stands is his.",
4852: "*Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam* (Matthew 26:64). Bound before the council, he names himself with the name Enoch heard named before the sun and the stars were made. The high priest called it blasphemy. But the Sanhedrin did not name the Son; the Father did, before the creation of the world — and the Father's naming is the one that stands when the council's has been forgotten.",
4898: "*All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). He says it as the firstfruits of the resurrection, three days after the earth was handed what it could not keep. Enoch saw the day the earth gives back what was entrusted to it and Sheol gives back what it received. The one who walked out of the tomb is the proof that Sheol gives back; the power he announces is the power of the one the earth could not hold.",
4899: "*All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Power to do what? Enoch says: *he shall choose the righteous and holy from among them.* The gathering is wide and the choosing comes after it — the wheat gathered out of all nations and then sifted, chaff from kernel, goats from sheep (Ezekiel 20:37–38; Matthew 25:32). The one who does the sifting is the one to whom all power was given. The tares were never wheat; the sifting is of the wheat, and he does it himself.",
7878: "*I am: and ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power* (Mark 14:62). Enoch was told the Son of Adam's lot has *the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* The right hand of power is that pre-eminence. Asked by the council who he was, the King answered with the title the angel gave Enoch — and claimed the seat that goes with it.",
7917: "*When a stronger than he shall come upon him, and overcome him, he taketh from him all his armour wherein he trusted, and divideth his spoils* (Luke 11:22). The strong man has been overcome before. Raphael was sent to bind Azazel hand and foot and cast him into darkness. The stronger one who divides the spoils in Luke is doing in Galilee what Yahuah (God) commanded in the days of Jared, and will do again when the serpent is bound for the length of the reign (Revelation 20:2).",
7943: "*Until the day that Noe entered into the ark, and the flood came, and destroyed them all* (Luke 17:27). Two outcomes, no third. Enoch records the instruction: Noah is to escape, and his seed is to be preserved for all the generations of the world — while everything else is destroyed. The days of the Son of Adam end the same way: the seed preserved, the rest swept away. The ark is not a metaphor for safety; it is the line between the two.",
7944: "*And as it was in the days of Noe, so shall it be also in the days of the Son of Adam* (Luke 17:26). Enoch tells what the days of Noah were: a warning carried to one man in Yahuah's (the Lord's) name — hide yourself, the end is approaching — over an earth corrupted by the Watchers. The flood came on a corrupted earth after a warning most did not hear. The days of the Son of Adam come on an earth corrupted the same way, after a warning carried the same way.",
7993: "*Before Abraham was, I am* (John 8:58). Enoch places the name earlier still: *before the sun and the signs were created, before the stars of the heaven were made, his name was named.* The Yahudim (Jews) picked up stones because they understood him — he was claiming to be older than Avraham (Abraham). He was older than the stars. The Formed one speaks his own name in the first person; Enoch heard it named in the third.",
15033: "*I saw a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit* (Revelation 9:1). Enoch was shown the pit before John was: beyond the abyss, a place with no firmament above and no founded earth beneath, no water, no birds — a waste and horrible place. That is the bottomless pit. The fallen star is handed the key to a place Enoch had already walked to the edge of.",
25558: "*Their names shall be blotted out of the book of life* (1 Enoch 108:3). Names can be blotted out because they were written first — and Enoch tells when: the Son's own name was named *before the sun and the signs were created, before the stars of the heaven were made.* The roll was written before the world. Chapter 108 takes names off it; nothing in Enoch, or in the canon, ever adds one.",
25627: "*In his days the angels of Yahuah (God) descended on the earth, those who are named the Watchers* (Jubilees 4:15). Jubilees dates the descent to Jared's days; 1 Enoch dates it the same way and adds the place and the number — two hundred, on the summit of Hermon, bound by an oath. Two books, one generation, one mountain.",
25629: "*There he writes down the condemnation and judgment of the world* (Jubilees 4:23). The commission Jubilees describes, 1 Enoch shows from the inside: the dream, the visions of chastisement, and the voice telling Enoch to carry it to the sons of heaven and reprimand them. Jubilees says he became the scribe of judgment; 1 Enoch is the judgment he wrote.",
25648: "*They began to devour each other* (Jubilees 5:2). Jubilees says all flesh began to devour each other; 1 Enoch says who started it. The giants consumed everything men had, and when men could no longer feed them, the giants turned on mankind and ate them. The devouring of Jubilees 5:2 has a face.",
25653: "*But Noah found grace before the eyes of Yahuah (God)* (Jubilees 5:5). What the grace did, 1 Enoch records as an order given to an angel: instruct him so that he escapes and his seed is preserved for every generation of the world. Grace found Noah; the instruction is what grace looked like.",
25656: "*He sent His sword into their midst that each should slay his neighbour* (Jubilees 5:9). The sword has a name in 1 Enoch: Gabriel, sent against the children of the Watchers to *send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle.* Jubilees reports the slaughter; 1 Enoch reports the command that caused it.",
25900: "*Till the day of judgment, on which Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) shall judge them with a sword and with fire* (Jubilees 9:15). The day the sons of Noah bound themselves to by oath is the day the bound Watchers are waiting for. 1 Enoch names it the same way — *the day of the great judgement,* and the fire. One day, two books, the same reckoning.",
25928: "*The unclean demons began to lead astray the children of the sons of Noah* (Jubilees 10:1). Jubilees calls them unclean demons; 1 Enoch tells you what they are. The giants born of spirits and flesh became evil spirits on the earth when their bodies died, and the earth is their dwelling. The demons troubling Noah's grandsons are the dead giants of the Watchers.",
25953: "*All the signs of the stars, and the signs of the moon and of the sun are all in the hand of Yahuah (God). Why do I search (them) out?* (Jubilees 12:17). Abram turns from the stars and, in the next verses, prays to be delivered from the evil spirits that rule men's hearts. Uriel showed Enoch those spirits: the Watchers' spirits in many forms, *lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods.* Star-reading was one of the arts they taught. Abram walked away from the art and asked to be kept from its teachers.",
26002: "*Over all has He placed spirits in authority to lead them astray from Him* (Jubilees 15:31). The spirits set over the nations are the spirits behind the idols. 1 Enoch names the worship — stones, images of gold and silver and wood and clay, impure spirits and demons — and the result: *no manner of help from them.* The nations were handed to spirits; Yashar'el (Israel) was kept for Yahuah (God) himself. The idols are not empty; they have tenants.",
26034: "*It was commanded and engraven concerning all his seed, on the heavenly tables, to remove them and root them out* (Jubilees 16:9). The judgment of Sodom was written before it fell. 1 Enoch shows the same pattern for the Watchers: their end was fixed — led off to the abyss of fire, to the torment and the prison, for ever. The sentence is written before the day; the day only executes it.",
29171: "*The end of all flesh is come before me, on account of their evil deeds, and behold I will destroy the earth* (Jasher 5:25). Jasher gives the word to Noah; 1 Enoch gives the messenger. An angel was sent in Yahuah's (the Lord's) name to tell Noah to hide himself, that the end was approaching and a deluge would destroy everything on the earth. Two books carry the same warning to the same man.",
60445: "*Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment* (2 Peter 2:4). Kefa (Peter) is summarizing something written out in full elsewhere. 1 Enoch gives the order to Raphael: bind Azazel hand and foot, cast him into the darkness, cover him with rough rocks until the judgment. The chains of darkness are these chains; the reserving unto judgment is this reserving. Jude 6 and 1 Peter 3:19 are reading the same book.",
141653: "*His angels he charged with folly* (Job 4:18). What folly? 1 Enoch names it, in the charge spoken to the Watchers' faces: you left the high, holy, eternal heaven, lay with women, defiled yourselves with the daughters of men, and begot giants. Eliphaz knew that angels had been charged with something. Enoch records the charge.",
}

# member notes: (thread_id, card id) -> new member note. Short: citation, exact live fragment, one pointer sentence.
MEMBERS = {
(27, 4255): "1 Enoch 48:2 — *that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The name given at Matthew 1:21 was named before the Head of Days.",
(27, 4257): "1 Enoch 48:6 — *chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world.* The Formed one, hidden before creation, revealed as Emmanuel.",
(71, 4390): "1 Enoch 46:1 — *with Him was another being whose countenance had the appearance of a man.* The Head of Days and the one beside him; the Son of Adam of Matthew 8:20 is that one.",
(71, 4392): "1 Enoch 46:3 — *This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness … whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The title by which Yahusha (Jesus) names himself at Matthew 8:20, given to Enoch by the angel.",
(30425, 4392): "1 Enoch 46:3 — *This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness.* The library's own naming of the Son of Adam beside the Head of Days — the figure of Daniel 7, named.",
(96, 4409): "1 Enoch 48:2 — *that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The one named before creation is the one with power on earth to forgive sins (Matthew 9:6).",
(115, 4455): "1 Enoch 99:5 — *they shall abandon their children.* The household comes apart in the day of destruction; Matthew 10:35 says the King's voice divides it too.",
(115, 4456): "1 Enoch 100:1 — *the fathers together with their sons shall be smitten And brothers one with another shall fall in death.* The seed war inside one house; *a man's foes shall be they of his own household* (Matthew 10:36).",
(125, 4481): "1 Enoch 46:1 — *One who had a head of days … And with Him was another being.* Father and Son seen together before the incarnation; Matthew 11:27 names their knowing of each other.",
(125, 4482): "1 Enoch 46:3 — *who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden.* The Son reveals the hidden Father, to whom he will (Matthew 11:27).",
(125, 4483): "1 Enoch 48:6 — *chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world.* Known to the Father before anyone else existed; *no man knoweth the Son, but the Father* (Matthew 11:27).",
(125, 4484): "1 Enoch 48:7 — *the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath revealed him to the holy and righteous.* The babes of Matthew 11:25 are the holy and righteous whose lot he preserved.",
(186, 4502): "1 Enoch 49:1 — *wisdom is poured out like water, And glory faileth not before him.* The Spirit put upon the servant (Matthew 12:18; Isaiah 42:1), seen from heaven's side.",
(186, 4503): "1 Enoch 49:3 — *in him dwells the spirit of wisdom, And the spirit which gives insight, And the spirit of understanding and of might.* Isaiah 11:2's spirits on the Elect One, with the righteous dead added.",
(188, 4508): "1 Enoch 10:4 — *Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness.* The strong man bound (Matthew 12:29) — done in Jared's days, done in Galilee, done again at Revelation 20:2.",
(188, 4509): "1 Enoch 54:5 — *These are being prepared for the hosts of Azâzêl.* The chains were forged before the King spoke of binding.",
(188, 7917): "1 Enoch 10:4 — *Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness.* The stronger one who overcomes and divides the spoils (Luke 11:22) is doing what Raphael was sent to do.",
(191, 4518): "1 Enoch 51:1 — *Sheol also shall give back that which it has received.* The heart of the earth returns the Son of Adam after three days (Matthew 12:40) because the earth returns what it holds.",
(197, 4535): "1 Enoch 6:2 — *let us choose us wives from among the children of men and beget us children.* The enemy's sowing (Matthew 13:25), told as history.",
(197, 4537): "1 Enoch 15:8 — *the giants … shall be called evil spirits upon the earth.* The tares' origin; another seed, not bad wheat (Matthew 13:38).",
(199, 4542): "1 Enoch 104:2 — *ye shall shine as the lights of heaven, ye shall shine and ye shall be seen.* The righteous shining as the sun (Matthew 13:43; Daniel 12:3).",
(200, 4544): "1 Enoch 48:6 — *chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world.* The secret kept from the foundation (Matthew 13:35) is the one speaking the parables.",
(202, 4554): "1 Enoch 100:5 — *guardians from amongst the holy angels To guard them as the apple of an eye.* The angels who guard the just are the angels who sever the wicked from them (Matthew 13:49).",
(224, 4599): "1 Enoch 48:2 — *that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* Kefa's (Peter's) confession (Matthew 16:16) recognizes a name given before the world.",
(30915, 4599): "1 Enoch 48:2 — the Son of Adam named before the Head of Days; the Father reveals on earth what he named in heaven.",
(224, 4600): "1 Enoch 48:3 — *before the sun and the signs were created … His name was named.* What the Father revealed to Kefa (Peter) (Matthew 16:17) is older than the stars.",
(227, 4613): "1 Enoch 51:1 — *Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* Why the gates of hell cannot prevail (Matthew 16:18).",
(371, 4678): "1 Enoch 10:8 — *the whole earth has been corrupted through the works that were taught by Azâzêl.* Why offences must come (Matthew 18:7) — and why the man they come by still answers.",
(371, 4679): "1 Enoch 19:1 — *their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray.* Leading astray is the offence; the woe is for the leaders, the led are victims (Matthew 18:7).",
(371, 4681): "1 Enoch 27:2 — *This accursed valley is for those who are accursed for ever.* The valley Enoch saw is the Gehenna of Matthew 18:9 — a real place of judgment.",
(372, 4684): "1 Enoch 90:6 — *lambs were borne by those white sheep, and they began to open their eyes and to see.* The Father's will that none of the little ones perish (Matthew 18:14): the lambs that can open their eyes do.",
(379, 4714): "1 Enoch 98:10 — *ye know no ransom.* Riches cannot save; the disciples' *who then can be saved?* (Matthew 19:25) already answered.",
(382, 4727): "1 Enoch 48:1 — *all the thirsty drank of them … And their dwellings were with the righteous and holy and elect.* Many drink; the few are those already dwelling with the elect (Matthew 20:16).",
(384, 4734): "1 Enoch 46:3 — *This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness … whose lot hath the pre-eminence.* The pre-eminent one came to serve and give his life (Matthew 20:28).",
(384, 4735): "1 Enoch 48:2 — *that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The ransom (Matthew 20:28) was settled before the world; *the Lamb slain from the foundation* (Revelation 13:8).",
(395, 4780): "1 Enoch 46:3 — *whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* The half of the answer the Pharisees did not have at Matthew 22:42.",
(395, 4781): "1 Enoch 48:2 — *his name before the Head of Days.* Why David calls his descendant *my Lord* (Matthew 22:43): the descendant is older than David.",
(397, 4791): "1 Enoch 99:2 — *Woe to them who pervert the words of uprightness, And transgress the eternal law, And transform themselves into what they were not.* The proselyte made twofold a child of hell (Matthew 23:15).",
(401, 4806): "1 Enoch 10:2 — *Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!”* The days of Noah (Matthew 24:37): a corrupted earth, a warning to the few, a day the many do not see.",
(402, 4811): "1 Enoch 57:1 — *coming on the winds from the east, and from the west to the south.* The coming of the Son of Adam fills the sky (Matthew 24:27); nothing secret about it.",
(402, 4812): "1 Enoch 57:2 — *the sound thereof was heard from the one end of heaven to the other.* Matthew 24:31's phrase, and the gathering it describes.",
(402, 4813): "1 Enoch 61:5 — *those who have been devoured by the fish of the sea, That they may return … For none shall be destroyed before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The four winds give back the seed they took (Matthew 24:31).",
(411, 4851): "1 Enoch 46:4 — *Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats.* The council that sentenced him (Matthew 26:64) will be raised from its seats by him.",
(411, 4852): "1 Enoch 48:3 — *His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The Father named the Son before the world; the Sanhedrin's verdict (Matthew 26:64–66) does not.",
(423, 4898): "1 Enoch 51:1 — *the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it.* The firstfruits walked out (Matthew 28:6); all power follows (Matthew 28:18).",
(423, 4899): "1 Enoch 51:2 — *he shall choose the righteous and holy from among them.* The sifting after the gathering, done by the one given all power (Matthew 28:18). The tares were never wheat; the wheat is sifted.",
(629, 7878): "1 Enoch 46:3 — *whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* The right hand of power (Mark 14:62) is that pre-eminence.",
(649, 7943): "1 Enoch 10:3 — *that he may escape and his seed may be preserved for all the generations of the world.* Two outcomes at the flood, two in the days of the Son of Adam (Luke 17:27).",
(649, 7944): "1 Enoch 10:2 — *reveal to him the end that is approaching: that the whole earth will be destroyed.* The days of Noah (Luke 17:26): a warning carried to one man over a corrupted earth.",
(665, 7993): "1 Enoch 48:3 — *before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named.* Before Avraham (Abraham), before the stars — *I am* (John 8:58).",
(2063, 15033): "1 Enoch 18:12 — *a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it.* The bottomless pit the fallen star is given the key to (Revelation 9:1).",
(5164, 25558): "1 Enoch 48:3 — *His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* Names were written before the world; chapter 108 blots them out; nothing adds one.",
(5189, 25627): "1 Enoch 6:6 — *who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon.* The same generation Jubilees 4:15 names, with the place and the number.",
(5188, 25629): "1 Enoch 13:8 — *I saw visions of chastisement, and a voice came bidding (me) I to tell it to the sons of heaven.* The scribe-of-judgment commission of Jubilees 4:23, from the inside.",
(5190, 25648): "1 Enoch 7:4 — *the giants turned against them and devoured mankind.* The devouring of Jubilees 5:2, with its cause.",
(5191, 25653): "1 Enoch 10:3 — *that he may escape and his seed may be preserved.* What the grace Noah found (Jubilees 5:5) looked like as an order.",
(5192, 25656): "1 Enoch 10:9 — *send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle.* The sword of Jubilees 5:9 is Gabriel's commission.",
(5263, 25900): "1 Enoch 10:6 — *on the day of the great judgement he shall be cast into the fire.* The day of Jubilees 9:15's oath; the same fire.",
(5264, 25928): "1 Enoch 15:8 — *the giants … shall be called evil spirits upon the earth.* The unclean demons of Jubilees 10:1 are the dead giants' spirits.",
(5276, 25953): "1 Enoch 19:1 — *their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray.* The spirits Abram prays to be kept from after turning from the stars (Jubilees 12:17–20).",
(5292, 26002): "1 Enoch 99:7 — *those who worship impure spirits and demons … shall get no manner of help from them.* The spirits set over the nations (Jubilees 15:31) are the tenants of the idols.",
(5294, 26034): "1 Enoch 10:13 — *led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison.* A sentence written before the day, as Sodom's was engraven (Jubilees 16:9).",
(6192, 29171): "1 Enoch 10:2 — *Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!”* The warning Jasher 5:25 reports, with the messenger named.",
(14877, 60445): "1 Enoch 10:4 — *Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness.* The chains of darkness of 2 Peter 2:4, written out in full.",
(35119, 141653): "1 Enoch 15:3 — *Wherefore have ye left the high, holy, and eternal heaven.* The folly the angels were charged with (Job 4:18), spoken to their faces.",
}
